From a25bf34730e2d49291fd0c6dc9b914276dc608ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ticky (Developer)" <ticky@dot.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:21:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S3 throughput: chunk every family along its candidate axis
 into ONE cross-family queue so no worker idles while work remains and the
 last family gets all workers; F1 routed through run_f1_parallel._score_pairs
 (cond_labels aliases both axes in run_search, so slicing it silently shrank
 the search); permanent candidate-count invariant that aborts on mismatch;
 chunked-vs-unchunked parity harness over all ten families; per-chunk atomic
 writes with sha markers so worst-case loss is one chunk; cost-weighted global
 ETA that degrades honestly; ceiling raised to 16 and the family-count clamp
 removed; QUICK_START corrected from measurement

